{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAxiomsPrimitive","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAxiomsPrimitive","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAxioms_implies_disjoint_stabilisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAxioms_implies_disjoint_stabilisation","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovAxiomsPrimitive.lean#L236-L244","doc":"The Markov axiom M3 (encoded via `MarkovTraceAxioms.tau_stab_factor`)\nis the primitive axiomatic input; the disjoint stabilisation\ntheorem `disjoint_product_factorisation` follows from M3 alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.disjoint_product_factorisation_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.disjoint_product_factorisation_real","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovAxiomsPrimitive.lean#L223-L229","doc":"Archimedean shim of `disjoint_product_factorisation`.\nCarries the explicit `(hq : 0 < q)` hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.disjoint_product_factorisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.disjoint_product_factorisation","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovAxiomsPrimitive.lean#L218-L221","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.disjoint_product_factorisation_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.disjoint_product_factorisation_gen","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovAxiomsPrimitive.lean#L199-L216","doc":"**Disjoint-product factorisation (derived from M3)**: two braids K_1, K_2\nacting on disjoint strands give the factorised joint trace.\n\nK_1 has trace τ_K1, K_2 has trace τ_K2; their joint trace after\nstabilising k disjoint strands is:\n\n  τ_M(K_1 ⊔ K_2) = τ_K1 · τ_K2 · z^k\n\nThis DISCHARGES the `MarkovDisjointStabilisation` axiomatic class\nused in `prop:categorical-chain-convergence-mechanisms` (Mechanism 2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markov_iterated_stab_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markov_iterated_stab_real","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovAxiomsPrimitive.lean#L183-L197","doc":"Archimedean shim of `markov_iterated_stab` — preserves the\npre-Phase-2 `(q : ℝ)` API surface. Carries the explicit\n`(hq : 0 < q)` hypothesis so the statement is phrased via\n`markovZax_real q hq` rather than the positivity-implicit\n`markovZax (Real.sqrt q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markov_iterated_stab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markov_iterated_stab","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovAxiomsPrimitive.lean#L175-L181","doc":"**k-fold stabilisation (Tier 2 generic-R form)**: under the\n`MarkovTraceAxioms u` instance, starting from a trace value `τ`,\nk applications of M3 give `τ · (markovZax u)^k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markov_iterated_stab_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markov_iterated_stab_gen","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovAxiomsPrimitive.lean#L167-L173","doc":"**k-fold stabilisation (generic-R / Tier 2 form)**: starting from a\ntrace value `τ`, k applications of M3 give `τ · z^k`, where `z` is\nthe abstract Markov-Jones parameter in any field. Independent of\narchimedean specialisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAxioms_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAxioms_real","kind":"def","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovAxiomsPrimitive.lean#L157-L163","doc":"**Legacy archimedean alias** preserved for pre-Phase-2 callers.\n`MarkovTraceAxioms_real q` is a `MarkovTraceAxioms` instance over\n`ℝ` with `u := Real.sqrt q`; existing `[MarkovTraceAxioms q]`\ncallsites that took `q : ℝ` should migrate to either:\n  - generic `[MarkovTraceAxioms u]` with `u² = q` (preferred), or\n  - the explicit archimedean form `[MarkovTraceAxioms (Real.sqrt q)]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAxioms.tau_stab_factor_eq_z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAxioms.tau_stab_factor_eq_z","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovAxiomsPrimitive.lean#L155-L155","doc":"M3: the stabilisation factor equals `z = u / (u² + 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAxioms.tau_stab_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAxioms.tau_stab_factor","kind":"def","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovAxiomsPrimitive.lean#L153-L153","doc":"M3: stabilisation factor. Adding one disjoint strand\nmultiplies a trace value by `markovZax u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAxioms.tau_identity_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAxioms.tau_identity_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovAxiomsPrimitive.lean#L150-L150","doc":"M1: τ(1) = 1 (normalisation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAxioms.tau_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAxioms.tau_identity","kind":"def","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovAxiomsPrimitive.lean#L148-L148","doc":"M1: scalar value of `τ` on the identity element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAxioms.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAxioms.mk","kind":"ctor","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovAxiomsPrimitive.lean#L146-L146","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAxioms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceAxioms","kind":"class","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovAxiomsPrimitive.lean#L121-L155","doc":"**Primitive Markov-trace axioms** as a Lean class via the\nexplicit-residual pattern. Captures the axioms M1 and M3 from\nJones 1985 / Wenzl 1988 that (with cyclicity M2, implicit in the\ntrace construction) uniquely characterise the Markov trace on\n`H_n(R, q)`; M4 is derived from M3 via the Hecke quadratic\nrelation, with the distinct loop value z₋ = z − (q − q⁻¹).\n\nEach axiom is encoded as a scalar invariant (residual / stab\nfactor) plus an equation pinning it to the required value.\n\n**Tier 2 generic-R form** (Phase 2 of the q-usage Hoefsmit\nmigration, PR #1640 / #1658). The class is parameterised by an\nabstract field `R` and an element `u : R`; the intended physical\ninterpretation is that `u` is a formal square-root of the Hecke\nparameter `q`, but the class itself imposes no `u² = q`\nconstraint — that hypothesis enters at the callsite for any\nconcrete instantiation that needs it.\n\nArchimedean entry points: `MarkovTraceAxioms_real q` (an `abbrev`\nof `MarkovTraceAxioms (Real.sqrt q)`) and the `_real` wrappers\n`markov_iterated_stab_real` and `disjoint_product_factorisation_real`\nbelow carry an explicit `(hq : 0 < q)` hypothesis so they avoid\nthe `q-usage-positivity-implicit` warning. There are no instances\nof this class on `main` at the time of this Phase 2 refactor, so\nno archimedean callers are broken. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovZax_legacy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovZax_legacy","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovAxiomsPrimitive.lean#L107-L119","doc":"**Legacy unsafe form** of `markovZax` — `Real.sqrt q` without the\n`0 < q` hypothesis. Kept for backward compatibility with the\npre-Tier-2 callsites; new code should use one of:\n  - generic `markovZax (u : R)` with `u² = q` for `[Field R]`\n    (Tier 2 — preferred; avoids `Real.sqrt` entirely)\n  - `markovZax_real (q : ℝ) (hq : 0 < q)` (Tier 5 archimedean\n    shim with explicit positivity)\nDo NOT migrate to `markovZax (Real.sqrt q)` — that still triggers\nthe `q-usage-positivity-implicit` warning since `Real.sqrt` carries\nno positivity hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovZax_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovZax_real","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovAxiomsPrimitive.lean#L80-L105","doc":"**Archimedean specialisation** of `markovZax` over `ℝ`, in **convention D**:\n`z_D q = q³/(q² + 1) = q² · markovZax q`.\n\n**Migrated from convention C 2026-08-26 (bean `qou-cxjq`).** This read\n`markovZax (Real.sqrt q)`, i.e. `√q/(q+1)` — convention C, excised by owner\nruling R1 of 2026-08-15.\n\nThe migration is possible in exactly this shape and no other, and that is a\ntheorem rather than a preference. `markovZax` is convention-neutral **as a\nfunction**; the convention lives in how it is *instantiated*, and\n`QOU.BraidKnot.no_kernel_instantiation_is_conventionD` proves that for every\n`q > 1` **no** argument `u` whatsoever gives `markovZax u = z_D q` — the\nkernel's real range is `[-1/2, 1/2]` and `z_D q > 1/2`. So convention D is\nunreachable by re-instantiating, and is reached instead by the *rescaling*\n`q² · markovZax q` (`QOU.BraidKnot.markovZD_eq_sq_mul_kernel`).\n\nThis is why the 2026-08-03 Tier-2 migration, which replaced `Real.sqrt` with\nthe generic kernel, did not make the convention question go away: it removed\nthe square root, which was its goal, and left convention C in place and\nharder to see.\n\nThe `0 < q` hypothesis is retained for backward compatibility with existing\ncallsites. Convention D needs no positivity — there is no `Real.sqrt` left in\nit — so the hypothesis is now genuinely unused rather than load-bearing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovZax","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovZax","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovAxiomsPrimitive.lean#L54-L78","doc":"**Markov-Jones parameter, generic-R Tier 2 form**.\n\nDefined for the formal square root `u` (any element of a field\nwith `u² = q`). The closed form `u / (u² + 1)` avoids\n`Real.sqrt`, works over any field, and matches the original\n`1 / (u + u⁻¹)` formula (equivalent by clearing the denominator).\n\n**The Markov KERNEL, not a Markov parameter — convention-C shaped, kept\ndeliberately for comparison** (bean `qou-cxjq`, 2026-08-26).\n\nThe old line here read \"Archimedean specialisation:\n`markovZax (Real.sqrt q) = markovZax_real q hq` when `0 < q`\". That is no\nlonger true — `markovZax_real` is now convention D — and it is removed rather\nthan left to rot.\n\n`markovZax u = u/(u²+1)` is convention-neutral *as a function*; the\nconvention lives in how it is instantiated. Convention C is `markovZax √q`.\nConvention D is **not** `markovZax u` for any `u` at all\n(`QOU.BraidKnot.no_kernel_instantiation_is_conventionD`: the kernel's real\nrange is `[-1/2, 1/2]` and `z_D q > 1/2` for every `q > 1`) — it is the\n*rescaling* `q² · markovZax q`, which is what `markovZax_real` now computes.\n\nSo: do not consume this as a Markov parameter. Use `markovZax_real`, which is\nconvention D. ","signatureChunk":0}]}